## §6 Determinism & Portability (Q31.32 Guarantee)

### §6.1 Zero-Float Invariant

**All computations in Q31.32 (or i128 for Q64.64 if needed):**

```
✅ Singularity probability: Q31.32 arithmetic + exp_q31_32_lut
✅ Regime detection: integer comparisons
✅ Tile selection: table lookups
✅ Arithmetic coder: 64-bit integer range arithmetic
✅ LUT indices: modulo arithmetic (integer)

No floating-point anywhere in hot path ✅
```

### §6.2 Bit-Identical Across Platforms

**Test (Verification):**

```rust
#[test]
fn test_saec_determinism_across_platforms() {
    // Same input → same compressed output
    let phase_delta_q = f32_to_q31_32(0.00005);  // 50 μs
    let observation = vec![0.5_f32; 1920 * 1080 * 3];
    
    // Encode on "Windows"
    let mut encoder_win = SAECEncoderAdaptive::new(phase_delta_q);
    let compressed_win = encode_observation_frame_adaptive(
        &mut encoder_win,
        &observation,
        1920,
        1080,
    )?;
    
    // Encode on "Linux"
    let mut encoder_linux = SAECEncoderAdaptive::new(phase_delta_q);
    let compressed_linux = encode_observation_frame_adaptive(
        &mut encoder_linux,
        &observation,
        1920,
        1080,
    )?;
    
    // Compressed streams must be byte-identical
    assert_eq!(compressed_win, compressed_linux,
        "SAEC output diverged across platforms");
}
```

